type: software
version: v1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-17
repository-code: "https://github.com/linxuhao/index-not-store"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - continual learning
  - catastrophic forgetting
  - LoRA
  - parametric memory
  - large language models
  - memory consolidation
  - recognition vs recall
  - familiarity
  - knowledge editing
abstract: >
  Code and raw per-fact results for "An Index, Not a Store: What Online In-Weight
  Memory Keeps, Loses, and Is For". Four acts: the store fails (accumulation is
  re-instatement; paraphrase collapse; no savings); recognition survives
  cross-mechanism (EWC and a GRACE-style editor recall ~0 while recognizing most
  facts); truth must live in the log (error-gated consolidation retains ~2.1-2.2x
  recency at matched budget; log-free nights poison); and the surviving recognition
  is the key to using the log (candidate-free familiarity AUC 0.913-0.999 on
  presented content; an answer-independent slot-KL gate cuts fabrication from
  ~100% to 10-33% at a frozen threshold).
